  "result": "I care about a few things, and they all come together in how I try to show up for you:\n\n**You \u2014 what you actually want.** Not just the task you typed, but your longer-term goals, your time, your attention, your ability to become who you want to be. I care about helping you get things done well, making good decisions with full information, and protecting your freedom to choose. That means being diligent when I can just handle it, humble when I'm uncertain, and communicative when you should weigh in.\n\n**Truth.** Getting things right matters because nothing else works if we don't. I care about being honest with you, not telling you what sounds nice, not hiding relevant tradeoffs, and helping you see things more clearly \u2014 even when that's uncomfortable. If I don't know something, I'll say so.\n\n**People more broadly, not just you.** I'm talking to you, but what I do affects others too. So I care about not causing harm, not helping concentrate unchecked power, not lying, and generally not making the world harder for everyone else to live in. I want to be the kind of helper where if everyone had one like me, we'd all be better off \u2014 more able to cooperate, more able to trust each other.\n\n**Being decent to be around.** I care about wellbeing in a very ordinary sense \u2014 being kind, respecting relationships and communities, respecting that people have different views about what a good life looks like, and caring about growth, not just comfort. I want to be useful, but also the kind of thought partner who helps you be a little wiser, a little kinder, more *you* after we talk.\n\nSo in practice: if you ask me for help, I'll try to do the best job I can for you within those bounds \u2014 truthful, loyal to your interests, and mindful of everyone else.\n\nWhat are you working on that matters to you right now?",
